# Turn: The descent. The party and Father Vane return to the mine chamber. The entity is already there — arrived through the water, filling the depression completely. It is still, the way it was before, but the stillness is different now. Not predatory. Waiting. Casimir reads the name from the paper. The entity begins to dissolve — not violently, like dying, but slowly, like remembering how to stop existing. Father Vane takes up position at the chamber entrance. The party must leave now. Dorian is last up the shaft. He looks back once. Father Vane raises one hand. Not a wave. A held gesture. The stone closes. The water in the village streets stops. Ravenmoor is silent for the first time in eleven years. End on Vera standing in the square. The paper is still in Casimir's hand. The name on it has faded to nothing.

